      "format": "python_code_unconstrained",
      "content": "class CheckAirConditionerOn(py_trees.behaviour.Behaviour):\n    def __init__(self, name, state_url):\n        super().__init__(name)\n        self.state_url = state_url\n\n    def update(self):\n        try:\n            response = http_client.get(self.state_url)\n            if response.status_code == 200 and response.json() == \"on\":\n                return Status.SUCCESS\n            return Status.FAILURE\n        except Exception:\n            return Status.FAILURE\n\nclass TurnOnAirConditioner(py_trees.behaviour.Behaviour):\n    def __init__(self, name, action_url):\n        super().__init__(name)\n        self.action_url = action_url\n\n    def update(self):\n        try:\n            response = http_client.post(self.action_url)\n            return Status.SUCCESS if response.status_code == 200 else Status.FAILURE\n        except Exception:\n            return Status.FAILURE\n\nclass SetFanSpeed(py_trees.behaviour.Behaviour):\n    def __init__(self, name, action_url, fan_speed):\n        super().__init__(name)\n        self.action_url = action_url\n        self.fan_speed = fan_speed\n\n    def update(self):\n        try:\n            response = http_client.post(self.action_url, json={\"fan_speed\": self.fan_speed})\n            return Status.SUCCESS if response.status_code == 200 else Status.FAILURE\n        except Exception:\n            return Status.FAILURE\n\n# Define the behavior tree\ncheck_ac_on = CheckAirConditionerOn(\n    name=\"Check AC On\",\n    state_url=\"http://localhost:8080/workspaces/home96/guest_bedroom/artifacts/guestBedroomAirConditioner/properties/state\"\n)\n\nturn_on_ac = TurnOnAirConditioner(\n    name=\"Turn On AC\",\n    action_url=\"http://localhost:8080/workspaces/home96/guest_bedroom/artifacts/guestBedroomAirConditioner/turn_on\"\n)\n\nset_fan_speed = SetFanSpeed(\n    name=\"Set Fan Speed to High\",\n    action_url=\"http://localhost:8080/workspaces/home96/guest_bedroom/artifacts/guestBedroomAirConditioner/set_fan_speed\",\n    fan_speed=\"high\"\n)\n\n# Create a sequence to ensure the AC is on before setting the fan speed\nensure_ac_on_and_set_fan_speed = py_trees.composites.Sequence(\n    name=\"Ensure AC On and Set Fan Speed\",\n    memory=True,\n    children=[check_ac_on, turn_on_ac, set_fan_speed]\n)\n\ntree = ensure_ac_on_and_set_fan_speed",
      "explanation": "The behavior tree is designed to increase the fan speed of the air conditioner in the guest bedroom by one level. Here's how it works:\n\n1. **CheckAirConditionerOn**: This custom behavior checks if the air conditioner is currently on by querying its state. If the AC is on, it returns `Status.SUCCESS`. If it's off or an error occurs, it returns `Status.FAILURE`.\n\n2. **TurnOnAirConditioner**: If the AC is off, this behavior attempts to turn it on by sending a POST request to the appropriate action URL. It returns `Status.SUCCESS` if the request is successful, otherwise `Status.FAILURE`.\n\n3. **SetFanSpeed**: This behavior sets the fan speed to 'high' by sending a POST request with the desired fan speed. It returns `Status.SUCCESS` if the request is successful, otherwise `Status.FAILURE`.\n\n4. **Sequence**: The sequence composite node ensures that the actions are performed in order. It first checks if the AC is on. If not, it turns it on. Finally, it sets the fan speed to 'high'. The sequence uses memory to remember the state of each child between ticks, ensuring that once a child succeeds, it doesn't repeat unnecessary actions.\n\nThe tree is structured to handle the dependencies and ensure the AC is on before attempting to change the fan speed.",
